The test `test_bmi160_emul_get_reg_value_range` is failing because the `emul_bmi160_get_reg_value` function does not return `-EINVAL` when attempting to read past the end of the emulated register map. This indicates a missing or incorrect bounds check within the emulator's read function.

The `BMI160_REG_COUNT` is defined as `0x7F`, meaning valid register addresses are from `0x00` to `0x7E`. The test attempts to read 1 byte starting at address `0x7F`, which is one byte past the valid range. The emulator function should detect this out-of-bounds access and return `-EINVAL`.

The fix involves adding a bounds check at the beginning of the `emul_bmi160_get_reg_value` function in `drivers/sensor/bosch/bmi160/emul_bmi160.c` to ensure that the requested read operation (starting at `reg_addr` for `bytes` length) does not exceed `BMI160_REG_COUNT`.

